    "Scouting Notes": "Reliever\n Fastball is mostly sitting in the 97 range with some ride.\n Also throws a sinker that has a ton of movement at times\n Slider is a good secondary, though it's not very consistent at this moment. Flashes of above average.\n Changeup is a WIP but I see some fantastic flashes and think it could be a great pitch.\n Control and command are both pretty iffy. \n There's a pretty exciting arm in here.\n Hope the Brewers will hold onto him this offseason by adding him to their 40 man. I'd even consider trying him as a starter, there could be 4 above average offerings",
